# Vercel Web Analytics Integration

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Nadav Anchors MVP project.

## Changes Implemented

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics@^2.0.1` using npm
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with resolved dependencies

### 2. Analytics Integration
- Added Analytics component import to `src/App.tsx`: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react'`
- Integrated the `<Analytics />` component at the root level of the App component (inside the fragment wrapper)

### Files Modified
- `web/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `web/package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
- `web/src/App.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Analytics documentation for Vite/React projects:
- Used the React-specific package: `@vercel/analytics/react`
- Placed the Analytics component at the app root level to track all page views and interactions
- The component is non-intrusive and will only collect analytics data when deployed on Vercel

## Verification Steps Completed

✓ Build completed successfully (no TypeScript errors)
✓ Linter passed with 0 warnings and 0 errors
✓ No breaking changes to existing functionality
✓ All lock files properly updated

## Next Steps

After deployment to Vercel:
1. Enable Analytics in the Vercel dashboard for this project
2. Analytics data will automatically start being collected
3. View analytics at: Vercel Dashboard → Project → Analytics

## Notes

- The Analytics component is lightweight and doesn't impact performance
- Data collection is privacy-compliant and doesn't require user consent for basic analytics
- Analytics will only be active when the application is deployed on Vercel
- In development mode, analytics calls are no-ops
